# Generated files are regenerated at a conflict, never hand-merged — see
# scripts/mergegen.mjs for why and scripts/prepare.mjs for where the driver
# is registered. A clone that has not run `npm install` falls back to the
# ordinary merge, which is the behaviour these files had before.
#
# ONLY a file its generator rewrites WHOLE belongs here. The driver copies the
# regenerated file over git's merge result, so a file that is only partly
# derived loses the incoming side silently — `docs/projects/README.md` and
# `docs/reviews/README.md` were listed here and are hand-written, and between
# them they ate the same index row twice on 15 Sep 2026 with nothing to show
# for it in `git status`. `test/mergegen.test.ts` now tampers with each target
# and regenerates, so a file that does not come back cannot be listed.
docs/ROADMAP.md merge=isocan-generated
